From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gondolin maintainers <FILL-IN-SENDER>
Subject: [PATCH] vhost_net: build without linux-headers on non-Linux hosts

hw/net/vhost_net.c includes "linux-headers/linux/vhost.h", whose own
system includes (<linux/types.h>, <linux/vhost_types.h>, ...) only resolve
on Linux hosts: meson adds linux-headers/ to the include path only there.
vhost-user is a portable feature, though (it can be enabled with
--enable-vhost-user on macOS and the BSDs, and memory-backend-shm provides
the shared guest RAM), and enabling it also enables vhost-net for
vhost-user-net, so the build fails in hw/net/vhost_net.c:

  linux-headers/linux/vhost.h:...: fatal error: 'linux/vhost_types.h' file not found

The only definition vhost_net.c needs from that header is
VHOST_FILE_UNBIND, used with the vhost-kernel (tap) backend, which is
Linux-only.  Include the header on Linux only and provide the constant
elsewhere.

With this, "./configure --enable-vhost-user" builds on macOS (tested with
10.2.1 on macOS 26 / arm64 with HVF; the patch also applies to master,
11.1.50) and vhost-user-fs-pci works against a vhost-user-fs backend with
-object memory-backend-shm,share=on.  Previously --disable-vhost-net
(and --disable-vhost-crypto) were needed as a workaround.

Signed-off-by: FILL-IN-SENDER
---
 hw/net/vhost_net.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/net/vhost_net.c b/hw/net/vhost_net.c
--- a/hw/net/vhost_net.c
+++ b/hw/net/vhost_net.c
@@ -33,7 +33,16 @@
 #include "standard-headers/linux/virtio_ring.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/vhost.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio-bus.h"
+#ifdef CONFIG_LINUX
 #include "linux-headers/linux/vhost.h"
+#else
+/*
+ * linux-headers/ is only on the include path on Linux hosts; vhost-user
+ * (e.g. vhost-user-net) also builds elsewhere. The value matches
+ * linux/vhost.h and is only used with the vhost-kernel (tap) backend.
+ */
+#define VHOST_FILE_UNBIND -1
+#endif
 
 void vhost_net_get_features_ex(struct vhost_net *net, uint64_t *features)
 {
-- 
2.x
